  "content": {
    "id": "p36-q1-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "1",
    "prompt": "A drawer contains six red, seven green, and eight blue socks. How many socks need to be selected to ensure that you have at least:",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p36-q1-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "one matching pair",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "4 socks",
          "worked": "Three socks could include one of each colour, giving no matching pair. With four socks placed into the three colour categories, the pigeonhole principle guarantees at least two of the same colour. Therefore, 4 socks are required.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 24
      },
      {
        "id": "p36-q1-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "two matching pairs?",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": {
            "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
            "version": 1,
            "blocks": [
              {
                "id": "p36-q1-b-short-result",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "6 socks",
                    "marks": []
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "id": "p36-q1-b-short-method",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "At most five socks can be selected without two disjoint matching pairs.",
                    "marks": []
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          "worked": "Five socks could consist of three red, one green and one blue, giving only one matching pair. To avoid two disjoint matching pairs, only one colour can occur more than once, and it can occur at most three times. Each other colour can occur at most once, giving at most $3+1+1=5$ socks. Therefore, six socks guarantee two disjoint matching pairs, which may be of the same colour.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 36
      }
    ]
  },
